    "long_instructions": "A program stores these 16 bits:\r\n\r\n```0110100111111001```\r\n\r\nThese bits describe a black and white image that is 4 pixels wide and 4 pixels tall. Each bit is one pixel (0 = white, 1 = black), read row by row starting at the top left. \r\n1. Write out the four rows, or describe the picture.\r\n\r\n<br>\r\n\r\n2. Suppose a friend sent you only these 16 bits and nothing else. What two other things would you need to know to draw the picture correctly?",
